join Valerie (Talking) left [animation="Fade In"]
join Lizzy (Talking) right [animation="Fade In" wait="true"]
Valerie: Ah, Elizabeth, how was your last day of highschool? I heard whisperings in the staff room that Holiday gave you a math exam.
Lizzy: It was pretty brutal.
Valerie: Hm. Well, math will only get you so far in your, shall I say, career. It was wise of you to focus on baseball.
Valerie: Speaking of, I circled the most useful classes in the fax I sent you. History, naturally, is my most recommended.
update Lizzy [mirrored="true"]
[wait time="2.0"]
update Lizzy
Lizzy: Val, is this really all there is?
update Valerie [animation="Bounce"]
Valerie: Oh, no, there are many different classes. I’m sure you could squeeze in an art class or maybe theatre to give yourself something fun to do.
Valerie: And VCR’s sports teams comes highly regarded. They even have baseball.
update Lizzy [animation="Shake X"]
Lizzy: No, not in school, I mean in life. Am I doomed to make every waking moment about killing some old dudes?
Valerie: The vampire lords aren’t some old dudes.
Valerie: They’re also old dudettes.
Lizzy: You must’ve had dreams outside of prophecies and the keepers.
update Valerie [mirrored="true"]
[wait time="2.0"]
update Valerie [mirrored="false"]
join Item (Watch) center [animation="Fade In Up"]
Valerie: This watch belonged to my great-great-grandmother, back when the Keep was first started.
Valerie: The eldest of every generation inherits that responsibility and the watch is a symbol of the struggle between light and darkness,
Valerie: And of course, helps me get to appointments on time. Plus it’s been known to be quite lucky.
update Lizzy [mirrored="false"]
Lizzy: Yeah the watch is cool and all, but...
Lizzy: Didn’t you want to do literally anything else?
Valerie: Hm.
leave Item [animation="Fade Out Down" length="0.3"]
Valerie: ...
[wait time="1.0"]
Valerie: No.
update Lizzy [animation="Shake X"]
Lizzy: So you’re entirely happy doing exactly what you’re doing and you’re going to do it for the rest of your life?
Valerie: I am.
update Lizzy [mirrored="true"]
Lizzy: I don’t know why I bothered asking.
update Valerie [mirrored="true"]
Valerie: There was a time in my life where I questioned what I was doing, if it was worth continuing my family’s duty.
Valerie: The Keep has it’s fair share of problems.
update Valerie [mirrored="false"]
Valerie: I believe it was my questioning that allowed me to break the rules and start working with you.
Valerie: Originally I was sent to Vermilion to observe and if necessary, eliminate threats to humanity, at my discretion.
update Lizzy [mirrored="false"]
Lizzy: Uh... Thanks for not... killing me?
update Valerie midleft [move_time="0.3"]
Valerie: You’re doing so much good here, all of you, Juniper, Barb, and even Noah.
Valerie: Without you and your friends, the Vermilion Event Horizon would have swallowed up half the country by now.
update Lizzy [animation="Shake X" length="1.0" mirrored="false"]
Lizzy: But what do I tell my parents? Sorry mom, I can’t go to Emmerdale because I have to stop Dracula from killing the president?
update Valerie left [move_time="0.3"]
Valerie: I see. You’re worried about losing touch with everyone.
update Lizzy [animation="Shake X" mirrored="true"]
Lizzy: Not exactly, but I guess that’s a little on my mind.
Valerie: They care for you deeply, Elizabeth.
Valerie:  Juniper isn’t the type of person to abandon those she loves. Barb is fiercely loyal, and Noah is enrolling in VCR’s arts program, so you’ll have a familiar face.
Valerie:  Besides, situations like these are exactly why portable telephones and electronic mail was made—even if I disagree with the discarding of paper post.
update Lizzy [animation="Bounce" repeat_forever="true" mirrored="false"]
Lizzy: But Emmerdale is half way across the United States!
Lizzy: What if they need me. I can’t kill a vampire through the computer. Not yet anyway.
Lizzy: What if some crazed fishman attacks Barb or Juniper sees a vision about impending doom and I’m too busy writing an essay about an old book nobody reads anymore—
update Lizzy [animation="Bounce"]
update Valerie center [move_time="0.1"]
Valerie: Lizzie!
Valerie: Thing are comfortable right now. And I’m sure we could spend another two or three years operating exactly as we are now, hunting vampires, saving people...
update Valerie left [move_time="0.5"]
Valerie: but there wouldn’t be anything to challenge us.
Valerie: We’d be stuck viewing the world through the lens of highschool student and teacher librarian, when it’s so much bigger than that.
Lizzy: Of course as soon as I’ve got the whole monster hunting thing figured out I have to go and refigure it all out again.
Valerie: You’re more capable than you think.


